// =============================================================================
// DATABRICKS PLATFORM VIEW — the layered "Databricks Data + AI Platform" map:
// Ingest | the stacked layers | Serve. Use it when the ask is the platform itself
// (a pitch, an overview slide, "what is Databricks"), or tailor it to an industry
// by retitling it and rewriting the item subtitles and medallion lines.
//
// This is JSONC for YOU to read. When you write `architecture.md`, emit PLAIN
// JSON (no comments) inside a ```json fence.
//
// What it demonstrates:
//   • A MATRIX slide, not a flow (`direction:"matrix"`): full-height Ingest and
//     Serve columns framing stacked horizontal layer bands. This file is the hand-composed
//     exception in reference/layout.md: every node carries an `at` offset, so each band,
//     chip and label sits where the slide needs it. Use nesting for any other diagram.
//   • Bands are framed `html` blocks (`<div></div>` + `style.fill/border/radius`,
//     `z:-2`) so they sit behind their content; a panel or chip INSIDE a band is
//     `z:-1`, never the band's own z (equal z paints in file order, and the
//     editor re-sorts the file). Each band has a heading `html`
//     (red square + bold title + one muted line).
//   • Product items = a `logo` with its OWN white icon tile (`size:[38,38]` +
//     `style: {fill:#FFFFFF, border:1, borderColor:#E2E8F0, radius:8}`) plus an
//     `html` title/subtitle beside it. One node per logo — never a second shape
//     behind it for the tile.
//   • Feature pills in a CSS grid inside one `html` block (Genie / Agent Bricks).
//     Each description is 2-4 words on ONE line (`white-space:nowrap`): short
//     phrases, not sentences. A grid column holds ~17 characters at 11px.
//   • Open-source chips = caption-right logos over a tinted `html` chip.
//   • The only edges are the Bronze → Silver → Gold medallion flow.
//   • Layer → layer flow arrows (`` → ``) in the gaps between the bands.
// Drop items the ask does not need; keep every band the same width.
// =============================================================================
